text:
Well, where to start?
So, we arrived at the hotel at 11 AM. the man at the front desk was very nice, we left our luggages there and he told us that the check in is at 2 PM ( we already knew that ).we came back at 2 PM and there was a lady. We had booked 3 double rooms.
we paid for the city tax, we left the warranty. one room was ready, two not. she told us that it will be ready in a FEW minutes. those few minutes were more than half an hour. I had my parents with me and they were  tired, I was feeling very sick, and the rooms nothing. So, don t you expect to receive your room at 2PM.
After all this trouble, we finally got our rooms ( they offered us champagne and chocolates for the trouble ) and surprise! the room was nothing like in the pictures. we had the sink IN THE ROOM. they gave us a room for people with disabilities... one room was normal in one side of the hotel, and the other 2 rooms were for people with disabilities in another side of the hotel.
What I really like at this hotel: 
-good location, near the arc de triomphe and tour eiffel;
-it has a very nice view at the tour eiffel;
-it has a nice garden where you can stay ( we ate there some pizza )
-right around the corner there are brasseries and restaurants;
-there is a carrefour shop at 3-5 minutes away;
-there is a pizza hut delivery ( you can eat there or you can go and take away ) at 3 minutes away;
-the breakfast was only 10 euro and totally worth it;
-the metro station is very near (3-4 min )
What I didn t like:
- the attitude of that lady from the front desk;
- the delay of the check in;
- the sink in the room;
- the fact that I payed  for breakfast in the first day 10euro and the day after, they wanted to charge us more ( like 78 euros for 5 persons ) but we payed 10euros after all. 
I m giving it 4 stars for the location

very nice and quiet boutique hotel; it is in a strategic position in the Marais near Place de Vosges;
although rooms are not big but they are very comfortable and bathroom is quite large;
in the morning they serve a hearty and great breakfast
